role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch7:2.6</span></span><p></p>The topology induced by <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d$\">$d$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> coincides with the original topology on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-4-finite\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-5-chart\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-5-chart</a> \\sketch Small coordinate segments have arbitrarily small Riemannian length, so metric balls are manifold neighborhoods. The short-curve lemma gives a metric ball inside every manifold neighborhood; hence the two topologies coincide. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#prop:dc-ch7-2-5","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#cor:dc-ch7-2-7","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-4","title":"def:dc-ch7-2-4","label":"def:dc-ch7-2-4"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite","label":"lem:dc-ch7-2-4-finite"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-5-chart","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-5-chart","label":"lem:dc-ch7-2-5-chart"}],"backlinks":[{"kind